An omission plan cites no stimulus trigger: when the scenario's trigger is the stimulus itself, the request the stimulus approach delivers, selected_evidence has no entry for it, because the stimulus is not a supplied observation or an evidence ref. Do not ask the plan to cite the stimulus as a trigger or to give it a selected_evidence role. A plan that cites no trigger observation is not defective for that reason; judge the trigger by whether the observation_claim branches and stimulus_approach state it. A cited trigger is a supplied observation of another operation's result.
